## Flexbox

Flexbox is a one-dimensional layout model that offers space distribution between items in an interface and powerful alignment capabilities.

```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}
```

## CSS Grid

CSS Grid Layout is a two-dimensional layout system for the web. It lets you lay content out in rows and columns.

```css
.grid-container {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: auto auto auto;
}
```

## Custom Properties (Variables)

CSS custom properties are entities defined by CSS authors which contain specific values to be reused throughout a document.

```css
:root {
  --main-bg-color: coral;
}

body {
  background-color: var(--main-bg-color);
}
```

## Media Queries

Media queries are a key part of responsive web design. They allow you to apply CSS styles only when certain conditions (such as screen size) are met.

```css
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  body {
    background-color: lightblue;
  }
}
```
